        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most people, the best Peloton alternative is a Schwinn IC4 with Peloton App+</strong>,
            or the identical BowFlex C6 if it is cheaper that day: the same classes for about half the
            three-year cost. If you want the screen and the automatic resistance, the NordicTrack X24 with
            iFIT is the closest Bike+ rival; if you want a better bike, the Keiser M3i, the Wahoo KICKR BIKE
            PRO or a smart trainer on your own road bike each beat a Peloton at something.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, price it with three years of membership, choose App+ rather than App One if you
            ride often, and be wary of any bike that only works when its maker's servers say so. If you
            already own a road bike,
            <a href="/best-smart-bike-trainers/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">our smart bike trainer guide</a>
            is the next place to look.
          </p>
